body:
For example, 
```javascript
class XParent extends HTMLElement {
  connectedCallback() { ... }
};
class XChild extends HTMLElement {
   connectedCallback() { ... }
}
customElements.define("x-parent", XParent);
customElements.define("x-child", XChild);
document.documentElement.innerHTML='<x-parent><x-child>';
```

The steps:
1. Push a new element queue, `eq1`, onto the custom element reactions stack (Step 1 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#cereactions)
2. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#insert-a-foreign-element for `<x-parent>`.
3. Create `<x-parent>` (https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#create-an-element-for-the-token with _execute script_ is false).
3.1. https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-create-element with _synchronous custom elements flag_ unset.
3.2. Add upgrade reaction into `<x-parent>` 's reaction queue (Step 6.2.2. of https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-create-element).
3.3. Add `<x-parent>` into `eq1`.
4. Push a new element queue, `eq2`, onto the custom element reactions stack (Step 3.1 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#insert-a-foreign-element).
5. Insert `<x-parent>` (Step 3.2 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#insert-a-foreign-element).
5.1. Try to upgrade `<x-parent>` (Step 7.7.2.2. of https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-insert).
5.2. Add upgrade reaction into `<x-parent>` 's reaction queue (Step 2 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#concept-try-upgrade).
5.3. Add `<x-parent>` into `eq2`.
6. Pop element queue `eq2` and invoke the reactions (Step 3.3 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#insert-a-foreign-element).
6.1. Invoke the reactions in `<x-parent>` 's reaction queue.
6.2. Upgrade `<x-parent>` (the reaction added in 3.2).
6.3. Add connected-callback reaction into `<x-parent>`'s reaction queue (Step 5 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#upgrades).
6.4. Upgrade `<x-parent>` (the reaction added in 5.2), but do nothing since `<x-parent>` is in `custom` state.
6.5. Invoke `<x-parent>`'s connected-callback (the reaction added in 6.3)
....

I guess we probably should ignore step 3.1 and 3.3 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#insert-a-foreign-element if the parser is created for a fragment, something like the step 6 and 9 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#create-an-element-for-the-token.

